  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1006 PM CDT Wed Oct 28 2026\n\nLight to moderate rain (and perhaps some embedded drizzle) will\npersist into Sunday as the shortwave trough drops southeast of the TN\nValley. Temperatures will remain on the cool side as a result of the\nclouds and precipitation, with readings staying in the 60s. Dew\npoints will remain in the lower to middle 50s. Temperatures will\nmoderate into the lower to middle 70s Monday and Tuesday. A stronger\nupper low/trough will move into the Plains Tuesday and lower MO\nValley through the western Gulf states on Wednesday. This will \nspread increasing upper level divergence and UVVs into the MS and \nTN Valleys. Low level southerly flow will increase substantially \nahead of the system, allowing dew points in the 50s to advect \nnorthward. A slower progression of the trough and cold front may \ndelay arrival in the TN Valley until Wednesday and it remains \nunclear if the trough will become more sheared out to the \nnortheast and not dig deeper into the Gulf states and southeast. \nIn either case, medium to high PoPs are warranted in the forecast \nby Wednesday. At this early stage, instability looks to be quite \nmeager with low probability of SBCAPE of 200 J/kg or higher, so \nthe threat of severe weather remains low, but we will continue to \nassess trends as we move forward.",
